Identify the years when the MLB All-Star Game was hosted in Toronto, including the specific venues and any notable details about the games held there.
The MLB All-Star Game was hosted in Toronto in 1982 and 1991. In 1982, the game was held at Olympic Stadium in Montreal, Quebec, which was the home of the National League's Montreal Expos. In 1991, the game took place at SkyDome, which is the home of the Toronto Blue Jays of the American League. The 1991 game was notable as it was only the second time the All-Star Game was held outside the United States.
