The actor who portrayed the first Alice on *The Honeymooners* was Pert Kelton. She was an American stage, movie, radio, and television actress. Pert L. Kelton was born on October 14, 1907, and passed away on October 30, 1968. She was the first actress to play Alice Kramden in *The Honeymooners*, which was created by and starred Jackie Gleason. Before her role in *The Honeymooners*, she was a prominent comedic supporting and leading actress in Hollywood films such as *Bed of Roses* and *The Bowery*. She also performed in a dozen Broadway productions between 1925 and 1968. Her career was interrupted in the 1950s due to blacklisting, which led to her departure from *The Honeymooners*.
