The J. C. Daniel Award is Kerala's highest honor in Malayalam cinema, established in 1992 by the Kerala State Chalachitra Academy, a non-profit organization under the Department of Cultural Affairs of the Government of Kerala, India. The award commemorates the contributions of J. C. Daniel, regarded as the "father of Malayalam cinema." It is presented annually to recognize outstanding contributions to Malayalam cinema. Recipients are chosen by an independent jury appointed by the Academy and the Department of Cultural Affairs. Awardees receive a statuette, a citation, and a cash prize. The award is conferred during the Kerala State Film Awards ceremony.
