Identify the category of drugs that mimic or interact with testosterone, including their mechanisms of action and common examples
The category of drugs that mimic or interact with testosterone includes antiandrogens and anabolic-androgenic steroids (AAS). Antiandrogens block the androgen receptor (AR) and/or inhibit androgen production, acting as functional opposites of androgens. AAS act as agonists of the AR, mimicking testosterone's effects. Common examples of AAS include testosterone itself, DHT, nandrolone, and other anabolic steroids. Antiandrogens include drugs like bicalutamide and flutamide.
