Determine the specific type of mechanical loom in question and its operational mechanism, particularly how it was powered by a horse or water wheel.
The specific type of mechanical loom in question is the **spinning frame**. It operated using a **bobbin-and-flyer mechanism**, where the spacing of the rollers was slightly greater than the fiber length to prevent breakage, and the nip of the roller pairs prevented the twist from backing up to the roving. Initially, the spinning frame was powered by **horses**, but later it was powered by a **water wheel**, which gave the invention the name "water frame."
