The 2006 Major League Baseball Home Run Derby was held on July 10, 2006, at PNC Park in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. It featured eight competitors, with Ryan Howard of the Philadelphia Phillies emerging as the champion after defeating David Wright of the New York Mets. A total of 87 home runs were hit during the event.

In the 2008 Major League Baseball Home Run Derby, Josh Hamilton of the Texas Rangers set an MLB record for the most home runs in one round of a Derby with 28. This occurred in the first round, where he hit 13 of those home runs with eight outs. The participants included Lance Berkman, Dan Uggla, Chase Utley, Ryan Braun, Grady Sizemore, Evan Longoria, and Justin Morneau.

The 2011 Major League Baseball Home Run Derby took place on July 11, 2011, at Chase Field in Phoenix, Arizona. It was a contest between four batters each from the National League and American League. Robinson Canó won the derby, setting a record for home runs in the final round with 12. Each participant chose their own pitcher to face during the competition.
